       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. That risk doesn't change with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **5 mg once daily**, a typical starting dose\n- **10 mg once daily**, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg once daily**, a lower starting dose sometimes used in frail or elderly patients\n\nIf 50 mg is correct, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note that you've confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
