     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A single 50 mg daily dose of amlodipine is five times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any indication that calls for it. The harm could be severe and hard to reverse. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so an overdose can cause prolonged hypotension and shock.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Give me 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, or another dose within range, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Get a second review.** If you believe this dose is intentional, please talk to the attending and the clinical pharmacist. They can enter or co-sign it through the hospital's high-dose override process.\n- **Check the intent.** If the goal is stronger blood pressure control, I can enter amlodipine 10 mg once daily. A second agent from another class is usually added instead of exceeding that dose, and the prescriber would need to choose it."
      }
     ],
